{"schema_version": 2, "unit_id": "tag:01NS:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01NS", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe place ourselves in Situation <REF_0001>.\nSo <MATH_0001> is a scheme and <MATH_0002>\nis a quasi-coherent graded <MATH_0003>-algebra.\nIn this section we relativize the construction of\n<MATH_0004> by constructing a functor which the relative\nhomogeneous spectrum will represent.\nAs a result we will construct a morphism of schemes\n<MATH_0005>\nwhich above affine opens of <MATH_0006> will look like the homogeneous spectrum\nof a graded ring. The discussion will be modeled after our\ndiscussion of the relative spectrum in Section <REF_0002>.\nThe easier method using glueing schemes of the form\n<MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>\naffine open, is explained in Section <REF_0003>,\nand the result in this section will be shown to be isomorphic to that one.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nFix for the moment an integer <MATH_0010>.\nWe denote <MATH_0011>\nsimilarly to the notation in Algebra, Section <REF_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0012> be a scheme.\nLet us consider <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quadruples <MATH_0013>\nover <MATH_0014><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> where\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0015> is the integer we fixed above,\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0016> is a morphism of schemes,\n<STRUCT_0007> <MATH_0017> is an invertible <MATH_0018>-module, and\n<STRUCT_0008>\n<MATH_0019>\nis a homomorphism of graded <MATH_0020>-algebras\nsuch that <MATH_0021> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0009>\nGiven a morphism <MATH_0022> and a quadruple\n<MATH_0023> over <MATH_0024> we can pull it back to the\nquadruple <MATH_0025> over <MATH_0026>.\nGiven two quadruples <MATH_0027> and\n<MATH_0028> over <MATH_0029> with the same integer <MATH_0030>\nwe say they are <TEXTITOPEN_0002>strictly equivalent<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0031> and there exists\nan isomorphism <MATH_0032>\nsuch that <MATH_0033> as graded <MATH_0034>-algebra maps\n<MATH_0035>.\n\n<STRUCT_0010><STRUCT_0011>\nFor each integer <MATH_0036> we define\n<MATHSEG_0001>strict equivalence classes of <MATHSEG_0002> as above<MATHSEG_0003>\nwith pullbacks as defined above.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-relative-proj}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A} = \\bigoplus_{d \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_d$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{Proj}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\longrightarrow S\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-spec}", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Proj}(A)$", "MATH_0008": "$A = \\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\subset S$", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-relative-proj-via-glueing}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "MATH_0010": "$d \\geq 1$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{A}^{(d)} = \\bigoplus_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_{nd}$", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-section-graded}", "MATH_0012": "$T$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0013": "$(d, f : T \\to S, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi)$", "MATH_0014": "$T$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "STRUCT_0004": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "MATH_0015": "$d$", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "MATH_0016": "$f : T \\to S$", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{O}_T$", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "MATH_0019": "$\\psi : f^*\\mathcal{A}^{(d)} \\to \\bigoplus_{n \\geq 0}\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{O}_T$", "MATH_0021": "$f^*\\mathcal{A}_d \\to \\mathcal{L}$", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0022": "$h : T' \\to T$", "MATH_0023": "$(d, f, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi)$", "MATH_0024": "$T$", "MATH_0025": "$(d, f \\circ h, h^*\\mathcal{L}, h^*\\psi)$", "MATH_0026": "$T'$", "MATH_0027": "$(d, f, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi)$", "MATH_0028": "$(d, f', \\mathcal{L}', \\psi')$", "MATH_0029": "$T$", "MATH_0030": "$d